<section class="content-ui-section" style="padding: 55px 0; background: #0b132b; color: #cbd5e1; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07);">
  <div class="container" style="max-width: 1060px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 15px;">
    <div style="background: rgba(15, 23, 42, 0.65); border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08); border-radius: 16px; padding: 36px 32px; box-shadow: 0 12px 30px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);">
      <span style="background: rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.12); color: #f59e0b; border: 1px solid rgba(245, 158, 11, 0.35); padding: 4px 14px; border-radius: 20px; font-size: 0.78rem; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.5px; display: inline-block; margin-bottom: 14px;">HANDOVER INSPECTION</span>
      <h2 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.7rem; font-weight: 800; line-height: 1.35; margin-bottom: 18px;">Destination Handover, Odometer Sign-Off &amp; Joint Condition Inspection for Bike Transportation In Sidlaghatta</h2>
      <div style="font-size: 1.02rem; line-height: 1.8; color: #cbd5e1;"><p style="font-size: 1.04rem; line-height: 1.75; color: #f1f5f9; font-weight: 500; margin-bottom: 12px;">When a two‑wheeler or motorcycle reaches its destination, the delivery handover must confirm that the vehicle’s condition matches the documented state at pickup.</p>
<ul style="list-style: none; padding-left: 0; margin: 16px 0 20px 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;"><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>This process, performed under daylight, ensures transparency for both the logistics provider and the customer, reduces disputes, and complies with standard operating procedures.</span></li><li style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; background: rgba(255,255,255,0.03); border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.07); padding: 10px 14px; border-radius: 8px; font-size: 0.92rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #cbd5e1;"><i class="fas fa-check-circle" style="color: #10b981; margin-top: 4px; flex-shrink: 0; font-size: 0.9rem;"></i><span>The handover is divided into three critical checks: daylight condition re‑inspection, odometer verification, and a signed condition sign‑off.</span></li></ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Daylight condition re‑inspection against pickup photos</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Position the vehicle on a flat, well‑lit surface to eliminate shadows that could hide surface damage.</li>
      <li>Open the vehicle’s storage compartments and inspect the bodywork, wheels, lights, and mirrors, comparing each element with the high‑resolution pickup photographs.</li>
      <li>Note any new scratches, dents, or paint chips; document them with timestamped photos taken from the same angles as the original images.</li>
      <li>Confirm that all accessories (e.g., helmets, lock, GPS unit) are present and in the same condition as recorded at pickup.</li>
      <li>Record the findings on the handover checklist, marking each item as “Match,” “Minor variance,” or “Significant variance.”</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Odometer verification against the LR bilty</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Read the odometer reading directly from the instrument cluster, ensuring the display is clear and free of glare.</li>
      <li>Cross‑check this reading with the mileage recorded on the Logistics Receipt (LR) bilty signed at pickup.</li>
      <li>If the mileage difference exceeds the pre‑agreed tolerance (typically 100 km for long hauls), flag the discrepancy for further investigation.</li>
      <li>Document the verified reading on the handover form, including the date, time, and the name of the staff member performing the check.</li>
      <li>Attach a photo of the odometer display as evidence, linking it to the LR bilty entry.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Signed condition sign‑off</strong>
    <ul>
      <li>Present the completed inspection checklist and odometer verification sheet to the recipient.</li>
      <li>Both the delivery agent and the recipient sign and date each section, confirming agreement on the vehicle’s condition.</li>
      <li>Provide the recipient with a copy of the signed documents and the photographic evidence for their records.</li>
      <li>Retain the original signed set in the central documentation system for audit and claim resolution.</li>
      <li>Update the transport management system (TMS) to reflect the successful handover and close the delivery ticket.</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
</ul>

<p>By following this structured handover protocol, logistics teams ensure that two‑wheelers and motorcycles are delivered with a clear, mutually agreed record of condition, mileage, and documentation, thereby safeguarding all parties against post‑delivery disputes.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>



